     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That's twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. The single dose of 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of GI toxicity and metformin-associated lactic acidosis goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nCould this be a typo? A few possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a brief rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest a pharmacy review first."
      }
     ],
